(5837704, 848058, 101536, '<td valign="top">Thank you so much to everybody who took the time out to vote and leave comments on this image.<br/> <br/>The ladybird appeared to have just woken from hibernation and I put it inside the tulip in my conservatory - it gorged itself on pollen and also got it''s shell well covered with the pollen - hence the insect looking a bit fluffy.<br/> <br/>After a while he crept through the petals obviously to find another hidey hole to wait out the rest of the winter - luckily I was ready with my camera and succeeded in capturing him and my best ever score since becoming a member a month ago.<br/> <br/>Thank you all again.<br/> <br/>AnnieK</td>', 'Thank you so much to everybody who took the time out to vote and leave comments on this image. The ladybird appeared to have just woken from hibernation and I put it inside the tulip in my conservatory - it gorged itself on pollen and also got it''s shell well covered with the pollen - hence the insect looking a bit fluffy. After a while he crept through the petals obviously to find another hidey hole to wait out the rest of the winter - luckily I was ready with my camera and succeeded in capturing him and my best ever score since becoming a member a month ago. Thank you all again. AnnieK', '2010-01-27 12:40:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5837729, 847137, 45243, '<td valign="top">Thank You for the explanation of your motivation for the shot and for posting it. While the capture is technically great, the "image" is very disturbing. I applaud your sincerity in raising awareness to an ugly slice of real life and wholehearted agree that saving one person is worth all effort.  I withdraw my very low vote (thought the image was for "shock" value).<br/> <br/>Good Luck with your series !<br/> <br/>Walter</td>', 'Thank You for the explanation of your motivation for the shot and for posting it. While the capture is technically great, the "image" is very disturbing. I applaud your sincerity in raising awareness to an ugly slice of real life and wholehearted agree that saving one person is worth all effort.  I withdraw my very low vote (thought the image was for "shock" value). Good Luck with your series ! Walter', '2010-01-27 12:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
