(5844495, 848223, 112107, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sfalice:</b></div><hr/><i> I bury my head in my hands.  HOW could this score below a five.<br/>Lovely child, lovingly photographed.  It''s a keeper.  <br/>Yes, I know the child is, so is the photograph.<br/>:-)) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you for the kind words Alice.<br/>(Mother)/Fatherhood does change our views (and votes) on children portraits especially when the subject is a baby. And if you consider that other people''s babies (especially newborns) are almost always ugly while our own babies are the most beautiful in the world, that might be the logic behind the voting. <br/>I did however expected to score much higher but I''ll have plenty of opportunities for that. I can always ignore all votes except from tnhe people who commented (and that is a 6.5) ;)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-30 13:19:33.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by sfalice: I bury my head in my hands.  HOW could this score below a five.Lovely child, lovingly photographed.  It''s a keeper.  Yes, I know the child is, so is the photograph.:-))  Thank you for the kind words Alice.(Mother)/Fatherhood does change our views (and votes) on children portraits especially when the subject is a baby. And if you consider that other people''s babies (especially newborns) are almost always ugly while our own babies are the most beautiful in the world, that might be the logic behind the voting. I did however expected to score much higher but I''ll have plenty of opportunities for that. I can always ignore all votes except from tnhe people who commented (and that is a 6.5) ;)', '2010-01-30 13:17:18.000000', '2010-01-30 13:19:33.000000', 0),
